# dependency-director Environment Configuration Template
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values before running the script.
#
# Variables are listed alphabetically within each block; see the detailed
# reference below for the ones that need more than a line.

# --- Configuration Variables ---

# GEMINI_API_KEY=your_key              # Gemini Developer API Key
# GITHUB_TOKEN=your_token              # GitHub PAT (Optional, highly recommended)
# DEPDIRECTOR_BOTS=[...]               # Custom bot JSON config (optional)
# DEPDIRECTOR_CACHE_DIR=               # Shared package cache dir (default: <tmp>/dependency-director-cache)
# DEPDIRECTOR_COMMAND_TIMEOUT=300      # Seconds per sandboxed command (default: 300, min: 10)
# DEPDIRECTOR_CONCURRENCY=1            # Concurrent scans (default: 1)
# DEPDIRECTOR_MAX_FAILED_JOBS=3        # Failed CI jobs whose logs are fetched per PR (default: 3, min: 1)
# DEPDIRECTOR_MAX_FIX_ATTEMPTS=3       # Max fix-and-test attempts per failing PR (default: 3)
# DEPDIRECTOR_MAX_OUTPUT_CHARS=24000   # Chars kept per output stream (default: 24000, 0 = unlimited)
# DEPDIRECTOR_MAX_OUTPUT_LINES=200     # Lines kept per output stream (default: 200, 0 = unlimited)
# DEPDIRECTOR_MODEL=gemini-3.7-flash   # Gemini model identifier (default: gemini-3.7-flash)
# DEPDIRECTOR_NO_SANDBOX=FALSE         # Disable sandbox-runtime (srt) sandboxing (optional)
# DEPDIRECTOR_OWNER=username           # Default GitHub user/org to scan
# DEPDIRECTOR_REVIEW_WAIT=0            # Min to wait for reviews (default: 0)
# DEPDIRECTOR_SRT_SETTINGS=            # Custom settings JSON path for sandbox-runtime (srt) (optional)
# DEPDIRECTOR_WORKFLOW_LOG_TAIL_LINES=50  # Lines kept from each job log's tail (default: 50, min: 1)

# Vertex AI Configuration (optional alternative to GEMINI_API_KEY):
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_LOCATION=us-central1    # GCP Location/Region for Vertex AI
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=project-id      # GCP Project ID for Vertex AI
# GOOGLE_GENAI_USE_VERTEXAI=TRUE       # Use Vertex AI instead of Developer API

# --- Detailed Reference ---

# GEMINI_API_KEY:
#   API key for accessing Gemini models via the Google Antigravity SDK.
#   Obtain a key from: https://aistudio.google.com/app/api-keys

# GITHUB_TOKEN:
#   Personal Access Token with full 'repo' scope access.
#   Optional, but highly recommended. You can retrieve this from your local
#   GitHub CLI environment using:
#     gh auth token

# DEPDIRECTOR_BOTS:
#   Override default dependency bots (automated dependency update tools like Dependabot and Renovate) with a JSON
#   array. Each entry must specify "author" (GitHub login) and
#   "rebase_command" (comment).
#   Example:
#   [{"author":"dependabot[bot]","rebase_command":"@dependabot rebase"}]

# DEPDIRECTOR_CACHE_DIR:
#   Directory holding the package caches (UV_CACHE_DIR, CARGO_HOME,
#   NPM_CONFIG_CACHE, GOMODCACHE and friends) used by sandboxed commands.
#   It sits outside the per-repo workspace, which is deleted before and after
#   every repository, so downloads are reused across repos and runs. All
#   repositories in a run share it; point it at a fresh directory per run if
#   you would rather they did not.
#   Example:
#     DEPDIRECTOR_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/depdirector-cache

# DEPDIRECTOR_COMMAND_TIMEOUT:
#   Seconds a single sandboxed command may run before it is killed.
#   Raise it for repositories whose test suite or dependency install is slow.

# DEPDIRECTOR_CONCURRENCY:
#   Number of repositories to scan concurrently. Use 1 for sequential.

# DEPDIRECTOR_MAX_FAILED_JOBS, DEPDIRECTOR_WORKFLOW_LOG_TAIL_LINES:
#   Caps on the CI logs fetched to diagnose one red PR: how many failed jobs
#   are retrieved, and how many lines are kept from the end of each. Jobs over
#   the cap are counted and reported, never dropped silently. Raise them for a
#   repository whose failures span several workflows or print more than a
#   screenful of context. Neither may be 0.
#   Example:
#     DEPDIRECTOR_MAX_FAILED_JOBS=6

# DEPDIRECTOR_MAX_FIX_ATTEMPTS:
#   Maximum number of iterative debug-and-edit cycles per failing pull request
#   before the agent gives up on it and moves to the next one.

# DEPDIRECTOR_MAX_OUTPUT_CHARS, DEPDIRECTOR_MAX_OUTPUT_LINES:
#   Caps on the command output handed back to the model, applied to stdout and
#   stderr separately. Output over a cap keeps its head and tail and drops the
#   middle, with a marker saying how much was dropped. Sandbox diagnostics are
#   read from the full output, so a violation is still reported even when the
#   line that triggered it is dropped. Set either to 0 to disable that cap.
#   Example:
#     DEPDIRECTOR_MAX_OUTPUT_LINES=0

# DEPDIRECTOR_NO_SANDBOX:
#   Set to TRUE to disable sandbox-runtime (srt) sandboxing.
#   Runs commands with host privileges. Only read-only diagnostic commands
#   are allowed via an application-level allowlist.
#   Example:
#     DEPDIRECTOR_NO_SANDBOX=TRUE

# DEPDIRECTOR_OWNER:
#   Default GitHub username or organization name to scan.
#   Can be overridden at runtime by passing a CLI target argument.

# DEPDIRECTOR_REVIEW_WAIT:
#   Minutes to poll for human review bot comments after pushing a fix.
#   Set to 0 to disable wait and bypass review checks.

# DEPDIRECTOR_SRT_SETTINGS:
#   Custom settings JSON path for sandbox-runtime (srt).
#   If unset, the default srt-settings.json bundled with the package is used.
#   Example:
#     DEPDIRECTOR_SRT_SETTINGS=/path/to/custom-srt-settings.json

# GOOGLE_CLOUD_LOCATION, GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT, GOOGLE_GENAI_USE_VERTEXAI:
#   Settings for using Vertex AI. Run 'gcloud auth application-default login'
#   to authenticate locally before running the agent.
